From 7cefdbc8feb55f5b8af8c469094c2bcd71e3ff65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:20:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] JOY Bus: a room's owner no longer waits for each GBA reply,
 and idle status polls are not all sent

In a room the lag model only needs a real reply a lag old (or when it has to wait for it), so the command goes into the adapter's line and the game goes on; replies are collected and sent to the room in order. While a waiting GBA keeps saying the same status, three polls in four are answered with it instead of being sent. On by default (GBLinkJoyPipeline).

